<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29029" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠσ-ηλεγής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγος, ἀλεγ-εινός</span>) Homeric epith. of
		death and war, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bringing bitter
				grief, cruel, ruthless</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος,
				πόλεμος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.325
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.154
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηγάδες . . δυσηλεγέες</span>
			<i>cruel</i> frosts, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				506
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσηλεγέος ἀπὸ δεσμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					652
				</span></i>
			; also of men, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					795
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γείτονες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.
					87
				</span></i>
			.</div>
